  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nepal Electricity Transmission Expansion and Supply Improvement Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Nepal Electricity Transmission Expansion and Supply Improvement Project (&#x201c;The Project&#x201d;) will consist of three components: A) Transmission system development, B) Energy Access improvement and C) Small hydropower plant rehabilitation component.  The total budget is USD 128 million, out of which Component A, B and C comprises USD 99 million, USD 12 million and USD 4 million respectively. Contingencies comprise USD 12 million. ADB will provide USD 75 million, Norway USD 25 million and the Government of Nepal/Nepal Electricity Authority (NEA) USD 28 million.  The project period is 2012-2017. NEA will be the executing agency.

Project impact is increased access to reliable supply of electricity. Project outcome is improved electricity supply. The target group is the population of Nepal.</narrative>
  </description>
